'' A SUBSCRIPT OF AN UNSIGNED TYPE NARROWER THAN THE INDEX is zero-extended, as fbc does:
'' tbl( b ) with a ubyte 158 is element 158. A static array's subscript went through the
'' untyped Coerce, which sign-extended -- element -98, out of bounds under -exx and a
'' silent read below the array without it (dynamic arrays and pointer indexing already
'' passed the subscript's type). tiko-rt's instr indexes its Boyer-Moore table by a ubyte,
'' so on text with bytes >= 128 it read stack garbage as shifts and skipped matches; that
'' is what made tiko-test's EXPECT-FILE-HAS fail intermittently on an executable.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/array-index-unsigned.bas -o tests/driver/arrayindexunsigned.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/arrayindexunsigned.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/arrayindexunsigned.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ubyte 7 7 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ushort 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2-d 9
